---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import GuideHeader from "../../components/help/GuideHeader.astro";
import GuideNav from "../../components/help/GuideNav.astro";
import Steps from "../../components/help/Steps.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/help/Callout.astro";
import RelatedGuides from "../../components/help/RelatedGuides.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "start", label: "Open your shop" },
  { id: "listing", label: "Create a listing" },
  { id: "confirm", label: "When a buyer messages" },
  { id: "orders", label: "After a sale" },
  { id: "money", label: "Getting paid" },
  { id: "boost", label: "Boosting a listing" },
  { id: "reputation", label: "Your reputation" },
  { id: "rules", label: "House rules" },
];
---

<Page
  title="Selling on NyasaBuy"
  description="How to open a shop, list items, confirm sales, deliver and get paid in Malawi kwacha on NyasaBuy."
>
  <GuideHeader
    title="Selling on NyasaBuy"
    intro="Open your shop, list what you sell, and get paid straight to your mobile money wallet."
  />
  <GuideNav items={sections} />

  <article class="guide">
    <section id="start">
      <h2>Open your shop</h2>
      <p>
        Signing up is free, and there are no listing fees or monthly
        subscriptions. Create your account, then open your profile and choose{" "}
        <strong>Become a seller</strong>. You will be asked for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your business name</strong>, the name buyers see on your listings</li>
        <li><strong>A phone number</strong> buyers and payouts can use</li>
        <li><strong>Where you are</strong>, so nearby buyers find you</li>
        <li><strong>What you sell</strong>, from the list of categories</li>
        <li><strong>How you accept payment</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can start selling as soon as you have applied.</p>
      <Callout title="Choosing a business name">
        <ul>
          <li>Use letters, numbers, spaces and apostrophes, like <em>Mary's Phones</em> or <em>Shop 24</em>.</li>
          <li>It must be 3 to 60 characters and different from every other seller's name. Capital letters and extra spaces do not make a name different.</li>
          <li>Names that imitate NyasaBuy, such as ones containing "Nyasa Buy", are not allowed.</li>
        </ul>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="listing">
      <h2>Create a listing</h2>
      <p>
        From your profile, tap <strong>Create listing</strong> and fill in:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Photos</strong>: up to four. Use clear, real photos of the item itself.</li>
        <li><strong>A clear title and description</strong>, honest about the condition</li>
        <li><strong>Category</strong>, which adds a few extra details buyers compare (size, storage and so on)</li>
        <li><strong>Price in kwacha</strong>, and the condition: brand new or fairly used</li>
        <li><strong>Where the item is</strong></li>
        <li><strong>How many you have</strong>. When you sell out, the listing closes by itself.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery</strong>: whether you deliver, and your delivery fee</li>
        <li><strong>Negotiable</strong>: switch this on if you will consider offers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Open <strong>Tips for a good listing</strong> in the app for advice on
        titles, photos and pricing.
      </p>

      <h3>Managing your listings</h3>
      <p>
        Your <strong>Seller dashboard</strong> lists everything you sell. Tap
        the <strong>⋯</strong> on a listing to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Edit</strong> its details, price or stock. From there you can also <strong>withdraw</strong> it: it disappears from search and your public profile but is not deleted, and you can put it back on sale any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Boost</strong> it (see below)</li>
        <li><strong>Delete</strong> it for good</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="confirm">
      <h2>When a buyer messages you</h2>
      <p>
        Buyers start with a chat: <em>"Is it still available?"</em> You will be
        notified. In the chat, tap <strong>Confirm availability</strong> to let
        them pay.
      </p>
      <Steps
        items={[
          {
            title: "Confirm it is available",
            body: "If you have more than one, choose how many. The number the buyer asked for is filled in for you.",
          },
          {
            title: "Set a delivery time, if you deliver",
            body: "Choose how many days delivery will take: at least 2. The days are counted from the day the buyer pays.",
          },
          {
            title: "The buyer pays in the app",
            body: "They get a Pay now button for 48 hours. You are told when the payment goes through.",
          },
        ]}
      />
      <Callout title="Keep your promise" tone="tip">
        <p>
          Choose a delivery time you can really meet. If the item has not
          arrived by then, the buyer can ask for more time or report a problem.
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <p>
        If a buyer makes an offer on a negotiable listing, you can accept or
        decline it. You are asked to confirm before accepting, so a stray tap
        never agrees a price.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="orders">
      <h2>After a sale</h2>
      <p>
        When the buyer pays, you get a notification and a receipt appears in
        your chat. Then:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pickup:</strong> arrange a time and place in the chat, hand it over, and mark the order as delivered.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> send it, then tap <strong>Mark as sent</strong> on the order. You do not need to choose a delivery time again. The one you agreed already counts.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The buyer then confirms they received it, and the order is complete. If
        they do not respond, it completes on its own after a few days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="money">
      <h2>Getting paid</h2>
      <p>
        Your <strong>Seller dashboard</strong> shows your money in three places:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pending</strong>: paid orders the buyer has not confirmed yet</li>
        <li><strong>Available</strong>: complete orders you can withdraw now</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawn</strong>: money already sent to you</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Tap <strong>Withdraw</strong> to send your available money to your
        Airtel Money or TNM Mpamba wallet. A minimum amount applies, and the
        app shows it. NyasaBuy keeps a small fee from each sale, and the
        amounts in your dashboard are always shown after that fee.
      </p>
      <Callout title="Changing your payout number?" tone="safety">
        <p>
          If you change your payout phone number or mobile money provider,
          withdrawals pause for about 24 hours. This protects you if someone
          else ever gets into your account.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="boost">
      <h2>Boosting a listing</h2>
      <p>
        A boost features your listing on the home page for a number of days.
        The price and the number of days are shown before you pay, and you can
        have a few listings boosted at the same time. Boost your best sellers
        when you want more people to see them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="reputation">
      <h2>Your reputation</h2>
      <p>
        Buyers can rate you after a completed order, and your profile shows
        your reviews and how many sales you have completed. Good habits that
        build trust:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Reply to messages quickly</li>
        <li>Describe items honestly, scratches included</li>
        <li>Deliver on the day you promised</li>
        <li>Keep everything inside the app</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="rules">
      <h2>House rules</h2>
      <Callout title="Never ask buyers to pay outside the app" tone="safety">
        <p>
          Do not tell customers to send money by Airtel Money, TNM Mpamba, bank
          transfer or cash in advance. Only payments made in the app are
          protected for the buyer, and only they are counted towards your
          earnings and reputation. Sellers who take buyers away from the app can
          have their listings removed or their account suspended.
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not sell fake, stolen or prohibited items.</li>
        <li>Do not post the same item again and again.</li>
        <li>Be honest about prices, photos and descriptions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <RelatedGuides current="selling" />
  </article>
</Page>
